# B-Tech Retail Sales & Performance Dashboard

![B-Tech Dashboard Cover](./btech_assets/cover.png)

A Power BI dashboard I built for a retail electronics chain to bring sales, profit, product, customer, store, and employee performance into one place — instead of everyone pulling numbers from different spreadsheets.

## The Problem

Sales Managers, Category Managers, Store Managers, Marketing, and Regional Sales teams were all working off separate reports, which made it hard to get a consistent read on performance. This dashboard gives them one interactive source of truth they can filter and explore themselves.

## Tools Used

- Power BI Desktop for modeling and report design
- Power Query for cleaning the raw data
- DAX for all the measures, organized into folders so the model stays maintainable

## Data Model

Built as a star schema from raw CSV exports:

- **Fact table:** `FactSales_2021` — quantity, unit price, discount, sales amount, cost, profit, performance
- **Dimensions:** `DimDate`, `DimCustomer` (governorate/country), `DimProduct` (category, sub-category, brand), `DimStore` (city, region, store type), `DimEmployee` (department), `DimPromotion`, `GovernorateGeo`, `StoreTargets`

Measures are grouped into display folders: Orders, Profit, Product, Customer, Store, Employee, Promotion, and Geographic.

## What's in the Report

| Page | What it shows |
|---|---|
| Entrance Page | Intro/landing screen |
| Landing Page | Navigation hub to the rest of the report |
| Overview | Company-wide sales and profit KPIs, YoY trend |
| Sales Manager | Sales performance by region, category, and time |
| Profit | Margin and profitability breakdown |
| Product | Performance by category, sub-category, and brand |
| Customer | Customer segmentation and behavior |
| Store | Store performance against yearly targets |
| Employee | Productivity by employee and department |

## A Few Things That Came Out of the Analysis

- Found which product categories and regions were actually driving profit, not just revenue
- Flagged stores that were falling short of their yearly targets so it's easy to follow up
- Tracked sales year-over-year to catch seasonal patterns early
- Cleaned up formatting across all the pages so numbers read consistently no matter which page you're on


